  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Requirements**\n\nI\'ve made progress on outlining the font requirements. Currently, my focus is on integrating the necessary fonts and icons for the project. Specifically, I\'ve identified the need for Google Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans and Inter, along with Material Symbols Outlined and Lucide React icons. These elements will be integrated into the `index.html` file.\n\n\n**Mapping Design Colors**\n\nI\'m now mapping the design theme and color palette. I have the YAML design spec. I\'m focusing on defining custom CSS variables or Tailwind CSS v4 styling rules to reflect these exact color values, font families, and utility classes in the implementation.\n\n\n**Defining Color Variables**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining CSS variables for the color palette within `src/index.css`. I\'m leaning towards using standard CSS variables or `@theme` declarations in Tailwind v4 to capture the specified color values from the design spec, which include variables for `on-tertiary`, `tertiary-container`, and more. My goal is to ensure the provided Tailwind classes like `bg-surface-container-low` and `text-primary` work flawlessly with the new styling.\n\n\n**Outlining Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m now outlining key feature integrations. I\'ve been thinking about utility classes like `border-outline-variant/20`, and font classes such as `font-display-lg`, `font-body-md`, and more to create a comprehensive list of design system classes. I\'m focusing on features such as an interactive navigation bar, hero section, and trust metrics. I\'m planning to use these to create user flows with interactive elements.\n\n\n**Planning Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m now outlining some core features. I\'m focusing on \"Trust Metrics\" with values like \"5k+ Happy Pets\" and \"12k Therapy Sessions,\" ideally with animated counters or badges. I\'m also planning to build filterable categories and rich interactive condition cards for treatments such as Arthritis and Hip Dysplasia. Each condition will open a detailed modal or drawer.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Modules**\n\nI\'m now outlining modules for the site. I\'m building out sections for service modalities, success stories, and our specialists. The services grid will be interactive, and I\'m planning patient case studies with progress sliders. I also want to include profiles of our specialists and a clinic gallery with a lightbox for images.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 596556214
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
